("ebola-outbreak-kenya-explained","Ebola reaches Kenya: what's happening and what it means for you","Kenya has confirmed seven Bundibugyo Ebola cases, all found in quarantine, as DR Congo's outbreak passes 9,000 cases. What it is, why it's trending and where to follow official updates.","world","ebola-outbreak-2026","Ebola reaches Kenya","Ebola",
[("ECDC: outbreak update","https://www.ecdc.europa.eu/en/ebola-outbreak-democratic-republic-congo-and-uganda"),("WHO Africa: Kenya's first case","https://www.afro.who.int/countries/kenya/news/kenya-confirms-first-imported-bundibugyo-virus-disease-case-who-supports-control-efforts"),("WHO Africa: Kenya response","https://www.afro.who.int/countries/kenya/news/who-supports-kenyas-ebola-response-third-case-found-early-quarantine"),("Willow Health Media: 4 new cases in quarantine","https://willowhealthmedia.org/ministry-maintains-confidence-in-response-as-four-new-ebola-cases-detected-in-quarantine/"),("CDC: returning travelers","https://www.cdc.gov/ebola/situation-summary/returning-travelers.html"),("CDC travel health notice","https://wwwnc.cdc.gov/travel/notices/level2/ebola-drc-uganda")],
"""<p>If "Ebola" popped up in your feed this weekend, here's the calm, sourced version. <b>Kenya has confirmed seven cases of Bundibugyo virus disease</b>, a type of Ebola, including one death, and every single new case was found in people who were <b>already in quarantine</b>. Health officials there say there's no sign of community spread. The much bigger outbreak is in DR Congo.</p>
<h2>What it is</h2>
<p>Ebola disease is caused by a handful of related viruses. This outbreak is <b>Bundibugyo virus</b>, first reported in DR Congo on May 15, 2026. By October 15, ECDC counted <b>9,277 confirmed cases and 4,478 deaths</b> there, across seven provinces, with 2,486 people recovered. Kenya's chain started with one traveler who had lived in DR Congo, flew into Nairobi on October 3 by way of Kampala and died on October 5, per WHO. His relatives and three health workers who cared for him before anyone knew he had Ebola make up the rest of Kenya's cases.</p>
<table><tr><th>DR Congo (ECDC, Oct 15)</th><td>9,277 confirmed cases, 4,478 deaths</td></tr><tr><th>Kenya (Ministry of Health, Oct 17)</th><td>7 confirmed cases, 1 death</td></tr><tr><th>Kenya contacts traced</th><td>128 of 130, all in quarantine</td></tr><tr><th>U.S. travel</th><td>No U.S.-bound commercial flights for anyone in DR Congo in the past 21 days (CDC)</td></tr></table>
<h2>Why it's trending</h2>
<p>Four new Kenyan cases were announced on October 17, the outbreak's first real foothold outside central Africa this fall, and news reports say DR Congo's outbreak may have reached an eighth province. That combination sent searches climbing in the U.S. The reassuring part: Ebola isn't airborne, it spreads through direct contact with body fluids of someone who's sick, and Kenya's quarantine net is catching cases early. Our <a href="/world/ebola-outbreak-2026/">Ebola outbreak 2026 guide</a> has the full facts table and FAQ.</p>
<h2>What it means for you</h2>
<p>For most people in the U.S., nothing changes day to day. If you're traveling, the CDC's rules matter: anyone who was in DR Congo within 21 days can't board a commercial flight to the U.S., and U.S. citizens arriving from Uganda or South Sudan get routed through Dulles, Atlanta or JFK for screening. Feeling sick after time in an affected country? Isolate and call your health department before heading to a clinic. And while you're thinking about health, it's a great week to get your <a href="/health/vaccines/">flu shot</a>.</p>
<p class="warn">General information, not medical advice. Follow your doctor, your local health department and the CDC.</p>
<h2>Where to follow it</h2>
<p>For numbers, stick with the official sources: ECDC's weekday updates, WHO Africa, Kenya's Ministry of Health and the CDC's Ebola pages. On social, the #Ebola hashtag moves fast and rumors move faster, so check claims against those sources. More world news lives on our <a href="/world/">World hub</a>, next to the <a href="/world/middle-east/">Middle East</a> and <a href="/world/ukraine-russia/">Ukraine</a> pages.</p>"""),
("iphone-duo-launch-week-explained","iPhone Duo launch week: is Apple's $1,999 foldable worth it?","Apple's first foldable iPhone arrives Friday, Oct 23. What it is, why everyone's talking about it, the trade-offs and where to follow launch day.","tech-ai","iphone-duo","iPhone Duo arrives Friday","iPhoneDuo",
[("Apple Newsroom","https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/open-up-to-new-possibilities-with-iphone-duo/"),("MacRumors: pre-orders and pricing","https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/15/iphone-duo-pre-orders-and-release-date/"),("MacRumors: the trade-offs","https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/14/iphone-duo-compromises/"),("Tom's Guide hands-on","https://www.tomsguide.com/phones/iphones/iphone-duo-hands-on-apple-nailed-it-and-just-put-everyone-else-on-notice")],
"""<p>The phone people have been joking about for a decade is finally real. <b>iPhone Duo</b>, Apple's first foldable, lands in stores <b>Friday, October 23</b>, and it's already the most argued-about gadget of the fall. Here's the friendly rundown before you hit "Buy."</p>
<h2>What it is</h2>
<p>Closed, it's a compact phone with a <b>5.4-inch</b> outer screen. Open it like a book and you get a <b>7.6-inch</b> inner display, which Apple says is 50 percent larger than the iPhone 18 Pro Max's. Inside is the same <b>A20 Pro</b> chip as the 18 Pro, there's a 48MP main camera and a 48MP ultra wide, and it's rated IP68. Colors are Star White and Night Sky.</p>
<table><tr><th>256GB</th><td>$1,999</td></tr><tr><th>512GB</th><td>$2,199</td></tr><tr><th>1TB</th><td>$2,599</td></tr><tr><th>2TB</th><td>$3,199</td></tr></table>
<h2>Why it's trending</h2>
<p>Two words: <b>the price</b>. It's $800 more than an iPhone 18 Pro with the same storage, and MacRumors found almost 40 things you give up, including Face ID (it uses Touch ID), the Action button and a dedicated telephoto camera. On the flip side, early hands-ons from Tom's Guide and Bloomberg were glowing about the hinge, the barely-there crease and how good iOS feels on the big screen. So the internet is split, and that's exactly what keeps a launch trending. Pre-order wait times are already long, per MacRumors. Our <a href="/tech-ai/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo guide</a> has every spec and FAQ.</p>
<h2>Should you buy one?</h2>
<p>Our take: buy it if you'll unfold it every day, for reading, two apps side by side, photo editing or movies on the go. Skip it if you mostly use your phone closed or love zoom shots. Either way, try one in a store, closed and open, before you commit. Trade-in credit runs $175 to $885 for an iPhone 13 or newer.</p>
<h2>Where to follow it</h2>
<p>Apple Newsroom has the official details, and MacRumors and Tom's Guide will have full reviews and launch-day reports. On social, the #iPhoneDuo tag will be packed with unboxings by Friday. More tech lives on our <a href="/tech-ai/">Tech & AI hub</a>, including the <a href="/tech-ai/ai-models/">AI model race</a>, and the <a href="/business/earnings/">earnings calendar</a> covers the week's big reports.</p>"""),
